=== Degenerate points -> E_H+ ===
c=0 gives X=c^2=0, Y=+-q*w -> the point P=(0,q*w) and -P. P is the rank-1 GENERATOR.
So the 8 degenerate points sit over {+-P} subset E_H+(Q) = <P> + tors.

=== What the MW-sieve needs, and whether PARI can do it ===
(1) J(V_q)(Q) generators: HAVE them (P on E_H+ rank1 + torsion on 5 factors). OK in PARI.
(2) Abel-Jacobi map V_q(Q) -> J(V_q)(Q): need a working model of the genus-5 curve.
    V_q is NON-HYPERELLIPTIC genus 5. PARI has hyperell* only (genus-2/hyperell).
    -> NO native Jacobian / Abel-Jacobi for non-hyperelliptic curves in PARI.
(3) Factored route: use the 5 elliptic quotient maps phi_i : V_q -> E_i.
    Each phi_i IS explicit. We CAN reduce mod p and push V_q(F_p) into prod E_i(F_p).
    This is the ONLY PARI-feasible sieve. Tested in 03_*.gp.
